WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.176 --> 00:00:01.009
(audience cheering)
- [Kelly] Oh no!

00:00:01.009 --> 00:00:01.842
Look at those legs!

00:00:01.842 --> 00:00:02.675
- [Nick] Oh my goodness.

00:00:02.675 --> 00:00:03.508
- [AJ] Hi, beautiful!

00:00:03.508 --> 00:00:04.341
- Oh my gosh, hello.

00:00:04.341 --> 00:00:05.310
I've been very excited.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:06.830
I always love when musicians come on.

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:07.663
It's just fun.

00:00:07.663 --> 00:00:08.940
It's usually a different conversation.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.710
I love you too, actors!

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.780
(group laughs)
I just mean like,

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:13.120
it's a different vibe obviously,

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:14.210
'cause we're all singers.

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:17.150
Anyways, so, you know
my band leader, Jason.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.735
- [Nick] Yes, I do actually.

00:00:18.735 --> 00:00:19.568
(audience applauds)
- [Kelly] Yes, yes.

00:00:19.568 --> 00:00:20.780
- It's so funny,

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:24.060
so, I had a failed attempt
in being a solo artist,

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:25.263
but that worked out for me.

00:00:25.263 --> 00:00:26.096
(group laughs)

00:00:26.096 --> 00:00:26.929
- [Kelly] I would not say failed.

00:00:26.929 --> 00:00:29.083
- [Howie] There's still time!
- And actually,

00:00:29.083 --> 00:00:29.916
Jason was my band leader

00:00:29.916 --> 00:00:31.850
and when I failed, then he just...

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:32.683
- Went over to you.

00:00:32.683 --> 00:00:33.916
- [Kelly] Thank you, for that.

00:00:33.916 --> 00:00:34.999
Thank you.
- [Nick] It worked out, right?

00:00:34.999 --> 00:00:36.810
- I was like, "That worked
out for me actually."

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:39.250
He's literally been my
best partner in music

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:40.530
and the only reason why I'm sitting here,

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:42.378
so anyway, he's so great!
(audience claps)

00:00:42.378 --> 00:00:43.770
- [Nick] He's amazing!
- He's so talented.

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:44.887
(audience clapping)

00:00:44.887 --> 00:00:46.010
- So, you guys..

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:47.790
Give it up for Jason
(imitates trumpet sound)

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:48.623
(group cheers)

00:00:48.623 --> 00:00:50.250
So, you guys started
almost thirty years ago,

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.130
so, what were those first days like?

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:54.400
'Cause y'all were like really young.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.370
- [Nick] Yeah, I was eleven
when I met these guys.

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:57.340
- You were eleven?

00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:59.460
- I was eleven.
- I was fourteen.

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:01.250
Yeah, I mean back in the day,

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:06.250
we used to ride on
basically like a Winnebago.

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:09.030
We were doing what they
called this ESM Tour.

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:10.670
So, we would go around
to like, middle schools,

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:13.630
high schools, gymnasiums, auditoriums,

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:15.880
and perform music that
nobody had ever heard,

00:01:16.948 --> 00:01:18.561
and we weren't signed yet.
- We did covers too.

00:01:18.561 --> 00:01:20.254
- Oh yeah, of course.
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah.

00:01:20.254 --> 00:01:21.300
Covers.
- [AJ] Covers, and...

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.860
- That's a hard play though to win over,

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:24.460
like a high school crowd, and like-

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:25.607
- Totally.

00:01:25.607 --> 00:01:26.814
- We have some great stories.
- Oh, teenagers can be cruel.

00:01:26.814 --> 00:01:27.796
(Brian laughing)
- [Kelly] They're mean!

00:01:27.796 --> 00:01:28.629
Yeah, no, that's what I'm saying,

00:01:28.629 --> 00:01:29.764
like even when you go to the school

00:01:29.764 --> 00:01:30.597
and you're in something with the school,

00:01:30.597 --> 00:01:31.900
they're still mean, like people are in.

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:32.870
- [Nick] Yeah.

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:33.703
- We were in...

00:01:33.703 --> 00:01:36.050
I think it was somewhere
on the East Coast,

00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:38.340
and we're in this auditorium,
we're doing our stuff,

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:40.540
and the entire sound system went out.

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:41.880
No mics, no nothing.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:43.225
- They pulled the plug!

00:01:43.225 --> 00:01:44.440
Like (imitates sound)

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:47.030
- So Brian, is basically
trying to get everybody

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:49.650
to calm down and to stop
yelling and screaming,

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:51.770
and they got really quiet and we just sang

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:54.900
straight acapella, and we won them over.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.124
- Oh, I love that story!

00:01:56.124 --> 00:01:56.957
I was hoping (mumbles)
(audience cheers)

00:01:56.957 --> 00:02:00.330
- They were standing up, it was amazing.

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:01.270
- You know what though?

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:02.760
That's sometimes the better play.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:05.010
Like, sometimes, 'cause
we always do big things,

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:06.810
I know people expect big shows from you,

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:09.770
but it is those moments,
and I know Floyd agrees,

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:11.410
but it's those moments
when you do something

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:13.920
like really I don't know,
broken down like that,

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:16.270
that really just showcases
the real talent behind,

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:18.140
you know, it's kind of a cool moment.

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:19.320
So, that's probably why,

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:20.490
just not everybody can do that.

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:22.180
- Well, it shows that you're real,

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:23.475
you know what I mean?

00:02:23.475 --> 00:02:24.500
- [Kelly] Yeah, exactly.
- I mean, what we do is real.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:25.868
All five of us singing together.

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:26.701
- [Kelly] Absolutely!

00:02:26.701 --> 00:02:27.534
- Just as you know as a singer,

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:28.495
I mean that's-

00:02:28.495 --> 00:02:29.328
- [Kelly] And that's really hard to do

00:02:29.328 --> 00:02:30.663
with a bunch of y'all.
- That's what we came to do.

00:02:30.663 --> 00:02:31.496
- [Nick] That's what
we pride ourselves on.

00:02:31.496 --> 00:02:32.329
- That's what we came to
do, so we just did it,

00:02:32.329 --> 00:02:33.223
and they were like... (gasps)

00:02:33.223 --> 00:02:34.056
- They were like harmonies.

00:02:34.056 --> 00:02:35.007
Since day one, we've
always picked up songs.

00:02:35.007 --> 00:02:35.840
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:38.280
- Boyz II Men, Shai,
Jodeci, Color Me Badd,

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:41.229
we loved the doo-wop evo
groups back in the days.

00:02:41.229 --> 00:02:42.062
- [Nick] Temptations...

00:02:42.062 --> 00:02:43.174
- We loved just picking
out all those harmonies

00:02:43.174 --> 00:02:44.110
and that's where we got
our signature sound,

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:45.190
it was based around harmonies.

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:46.023
- That's so awesome.

00:02:46.023 --> 00:02:46.856
I'm glad you had that

00:02:46.856 --> 00:02:47.960
'cause I'm sure we all had those moments

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:49.030
when things went like that,

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:50.977
and then we have moments
where they didn't go great,

00:02:50.977 --> 00:02:52.695
and you were like, "Am I talented?"

00:02:52.695 --> 00:02:53.528
(group laughing)

00:02:53.528 --> 00:02:55.017
And you have those moments
you're like, "Should I quit?"

00:02:55.017 --> 00:02:57.490
That was personally for me
when I saw you two perform

00:02:57.490 --> 00:02:59.720
at Madison Square Garden, I
was like "What am I doing?"

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:02.540
I was like, "I should probably quit."

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:04.350
Anyway, when Machine Gun Kelly was here,

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.840
he said he was a huge fan of you

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:08.290
and he also had this to say,
so we wanted to show you.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:10.040
- I went to a Backstreet Boys concert,

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.724
and I threw up on the first song

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:12.557
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:12.557 --> 00:03:13.790
because the girls were so loud,
they were screaming so loud,

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:15.910
I don't know how that equaled
out to me throwing up,

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:17.010
but,
(audience laughs)

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:17.843
- It's overwhelming!

00:03:17.843 --> 00:03:18.676
- I know it happened though.
- Yeah.

00:03:18.676 --> 00:03:21.290
- Like, they came down
on these hover boards,

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:23.770
and everyone was going so crazy

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:26.173
and I was going like,

00:03:26.173 --> 00:03:28.524
(mimics barfing)
(Kelly grunts)

00:03:28.524 --> 00:03:29.473
(audience laughing)

00:03:29.473 --> 00:03:30.404
(all laughing)

00:03:30.404 --> 00:03:31.237
- They're intense!
(audience claps)

00:03:31.237 --> 00:03:33.294
They're intense! They're loud!

00:03:33.294 --> 00:03:34.820
- Fortunately, we hadn't-
- [Nick] Awesome story.

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:36.830
- Started singing yet, so
that wasn't why he threw up,

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:38.160
- [Kelly] No!
- So, that's a good thing.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:39.200
That's a good thing.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.910
- He made it to the show.
- It's overwhelming!

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:42.030
He did, we talked about it.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.970
No, he loved it, but my point though

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:46.600
is like it's a different vibe
especially with boy bands,

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:49.689
like, it's a different
ball game, the fans.

00:03:49.689 --> 00:03:50.522
- It is, yeah.

00:03:50.522 --> 00:03:51.760
- 'Cause I've got a few
friends that actually work

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.680
on like y'all's tour, other peoples' tour,

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:55.310
do things like backstage
like meet and greet things

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:57.640
for y'all, and it's like a
different kind of fandom.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:03:59.060
Like, they really are invested

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:00.900
from a young age and it's loud.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:02.275
- It's loud, yeah.

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:03.699
- I mean, we like to say we have-

00:04:03.699 --> 00:04:06.528
(audience members scream)
I mean, it is loud.

00:04:06.528 --> 00:04:08.414
- [Kelly] It's like a different frequency.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:09.259
- What? What?

00:04:09.259 --> 00:04:10.765
- [Nick] We miss that. We miss that.

00:04:10.765 --> 00:04:11.598
- It's been years since hearing that.

00:04:11.598 --> 00:04:12.912
- It's been two years
since we've performed.

00:04:12.912 --> 00:04:14.074
- What'd you say? I'm sorry.

00:04:14.074 --> 00:04:15.350
- I know, but that's the
thing for a lot of artists.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:16.600
Like, everybody hasn't been able to do

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:17.433
what they've really wanted to do.

00:04:17.433 --> 00:04:19.550
So, are y'all so excited
about doing this tour?

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:20.720
- [Group] Oh, yeah.

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:21.912
- It's time.

00:04:21.912 --> 00:04:22.745
- Excited to get back out to the fans.

00:04:22.745 --> 00:04:24.891
- We've been chomping at the bit.

00:04:24.891 --> 00:04:25.950
(group laughs)
- Yeah.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:28.088
- Just sitting at home, eating,

00:04:28.088 --> 00:04:28.921
waiting to go out on the road.
- Driving our wives crazy.

00:04:28.921 --> 00:04:29.754
(all laughing)

00:04:29.754 --> 00:04:30.930
- [Kelly] Well, that can be...

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:32.100
- [Nick] And honestly, I feel now,

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:33.900
especially with the way
everything is in the world,

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:36.500
it's like entertainment
is so needed right now.

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:38.390
Like, our job is so important
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:39.918
- To get people's minds off this stuff.

00:04:39.918 --> 00:04:41.337
(audience applauding)
- [AJ] Music!

00:04:41.337 --> 00:04:42.419
- And just to be in a room

00:04:42.419 --> 00:04:43.930
and with people that you don't know,

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:45.590
and you're all like vibing on one thing,

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:46.580
I love that feeling.

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:48.020
- [Nick] Yeah, it's a
different kind of energy

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:49.630
and we thrive on that energy.

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:50.570
- [Kelly] Absolutely.
- You know what I mean?

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:51.810
Don't get me wrong,

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:54.110
our kids were so happy that we were home

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:56.130
for this last two years, but-

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:57.302
- Were your wives? (laughs)
- But our wives are glad.

00:04:57.302 --> 00:04:58.379
Our wives are glad now that
we're getting out of the house.

00:04:58.379 --> 00:05:00.230
- Our wives were like, "You
have to go back to work!

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:01.063
Please go back to work!"

00:05:01.063 --> 00:05:03.579
- I had two babies born
during that time, well prior.

00:05:03.579 --> 00:05:05.368
(audience applauds)
- Aw, that's so cool.

00:05:05.368 --> 00:05:06.201
I'm happy for you.

00:05:06.201 --> 00:05:08.780
They just added more dates
to their DNA World Tour

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:11.850
with cities including, Portland,
Cincinnati and Nashville,

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:13.070
shout out Nashville!
(audience members cheering)

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:16.380
Tickets for these and other
just added cities in the US,

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:20.030
Canada and Europe go on
sale this Friday, April 8th.

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:23.120
So, Kevin, what can the fans
expect to see on this tour?

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:23.970
What's different?

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:27.142
(group laughs)
(Kevin stutters)

00:05:27.142 --> 00:05:28.171
(audience laughs)
- He was like, "And..."

00:05:28.171 --> 00:05:29.048
- He likes to think about
things before he says them.

00:05:29.048 --> 00:05:29.881
- He's like, "What?"

00:05:29.881 --> 00:05:30.714
- He's a thoughtful man.
- I think this show

00:05:30.714 --> 00:05:33.720
is a great example of our musical legacy.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:34.839
- [Kelly] Oh, that's cool.

00:05:34.839 --> 00:05:36.400
(audience claps)
- Like, we're able to...

00:05:38.169 --> 00:05:39.002
We have...

00:05:39.002 --> 00:05:39.959
- [Kelly] Do you take people on that run?

00:05:39.959 --> 00:05:40.792
(audience continues cheering)

00:05:40.792 --> 00:05:41.860
- We have all the hits that
the fans know and love,

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:43.840
we have some new music,

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:48.840
and then some gems that were on the albums

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:51.910
that are our favorite that
we included in the set

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:54.380
that people are like, "Oh my
God, I forgot about that song!"

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:55.213
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:55.213 --> 00:05:56.750
- And we're excited to be
taking the show outdoors.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:58.230
- [Brian] Thirty-two!
(group chattering)

00:05:58.230 --> 00:05:59.063
- [Kelly] Did you just say..

00:05:59.063 --> 00:05:59.896
- Thirty-two songs!

00:05:59.896 --> 00:06:00.729
- Oh yeah, so the first half
of the tour is going to be..

00:06:00.729 --> 00:06:01.562
- Thirty two songs?!

00:06:01.562 --> 00:06:02.395
- Yeah, thirty two songs-

00:06:02.395 --> 00:06:05.353
- What?
(audience screams)

00:06:05.353 --> 00:06:06.186
- [Kevin] Ten albums..

00:06:06.186 --> 00:06:07.377
- Are they like medleys in there?

00:06:07.377 --> 00:06:08.528
- There's an intermission,
no, I'm kidding.

00:06:08.528 --> 00:06:09.361
- And they're choreographed.
(group chattering)

00:06:09.361 --> 00:06:14.234
- Oh my God, as a vocalist,
I just died. (chuckles)

00:06:14.234 --> 00:06:16.010
- And we're dancing the whole show too.

00:06:16.010 --> 00:06:17.069
- [Kelly] Oh my God!

00:06:17.069 --> 00:06:18.389
- [Brian] This is what we do, Kelly.

00:06:18.389 --> 00:06:19.760
We're a group, for sure.

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:20.820
- I love that.

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:22.740
That's awesome.
(group laughs)

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:24.100
No, I love that you're like dancing

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:26.470
and like meanwhile I'm like,
"I'm not going on stairs.

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:28.290
I'm not using stairs"
(group laughs)

00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:29.400
I won't even get on stairs.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:30.750
I'm like "Nah, people
ain't coming to watch me

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:32.010
stand on stairs, I'm gonna trip.

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:33.600
I'm not Beyonce."
(group laughs)

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:36.250
So, wait, has getting back
to performance and all that,

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:37.250
'cause you say you're dancing a lot,

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:38.770
so is that getting
y'all in shape for that?

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:39.710
'Cause that's a different kind of...

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:40.779
- We have to get in shape.

00:06:40.779 --> 00:06:42.170
I mean that's the thing
about the pandemic.

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:45.040
I mean I put on like twenty,
twenty-five pounds. (chuckles)

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:45.990
- Time off for us is like anything.

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:48.886
- I definitely didn't lose weight, Nick,

00:06:48.886 --> 00:06:50.240
so, yeah.
- [Nick] You look beautiful!

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:51.073
- And vocal shape though!

00:06:51.073 --> 00:06:51.906
Vocal shape as well.

00:06:51.906 --> 00:06:52.739
- [Nick] Yeah, that's a thing too.

00:06:52.739 --> 00:06:53.695
- Yeah.

00:06:53.695 --> 00:06:54.528
- I went the other way.

00:06:54.528 --> 00:06:55.361
- We started rehearsal like a week ago.

00:06:55.361 --> 00:06:57.480
We got about five
rehearsals under our belt,

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:59.810
and we got another month to go,

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:01.786
and then we'll be ready to rock.

00:07:01.786 --> 00:07:03.030
(audience cheers)
- That's awesome.

00:07:04.861 --> 00:07:06.280
Do you ever have that moment

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:07.930
where you haven't done a show in a while,

00:07:07.930 --> 00:07:09.840
and then all of a sudden,
I feel so awkward,

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:12.630
I'm like, "So I guess I'll
walk to this side of the stage,

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:13.850
and then I'll walk over here,"

00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:15.380
